From 6f4f974db73b53529cd8d785467929dcfcd7a874 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:08:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v1] watchdog: qcom: stop a bootloader-armed watchdog across
 system sleep
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On many Qualcomm platforms the bootloader leaves the watchdog running and
hands it over to Linux as WDOG_HW_RUNNING, so the hardware keeps counting
even though nothing has opened /dev/watchdog. In that state the watchdog
core's worker pings the device to keep it alive.

qcom_wdt_suspend() and qcom_wdt_resume() only stop and restart the hardware
when watchdog_active() is true, i.e. after the device has been opened. A
bootloader-armed watchdog is hw_running but not active, so it is left
ticking across system sleep while its keepalive worker is frozen. Once the
ping interval elapses the watchdog bites and resets the machine while
it is suspended.

Stop the hardware when watchdog_hw_running() is true as well, and restart
it on resume, so a bootloader-armed watchdog is handled across system sleep
too.

Fixes: 671cdde36e26 ("watchdog: qcom: Add suspend/resume support")
Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mráz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
---
 drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c
index 4eb1bf979012..a42c1af7d402 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c
@@ -362,7 +362,11 @@ static int __maybe_unused qcom_wdt_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct qcom_wdt *wdt = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
-	if (watchdog_active(&wdt->wdd))
+	/*
+	 * A bootloader-armed watchdog (WDOG_HW_RUNNING) is pinged by the core's
+	 * worker, which is frozen in system sleep: stop it too.
+	 */
+	if (watchdog_active(&wdt->wdd) || watchdog_hw_running(&wdt->wdd))
 		qcom_wdt_stop(&wdt->wdd);
 
 	return 0;
@@ -372,7 +376,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused qcom_wdt_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct qcom_wdt *wdt = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
-	if (watchdog_active(&wdt->wdd))
+	if (watchdog_active(&wdt->wdd) || watchdog_hw_running(&wdt->wdd))
 		qcom_wdt_start(&wdt->wdd);
 
 	return 0;

